{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type MediaPrompt = string | MediaPromptPart[];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L2109","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:2109"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prompt accepted by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVideo()"},{"type":"text","value":": a plain string,\nor an ordered array of content parts for image-conditioned generation\n(\"not like this "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(image)"}]},{"type":"text","value":", more like this "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(image)"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\"). Part order is\nmeaningful — adapters with native multimodal prompts (Gemini, OpenRouter)\npreserve the interleaving; named-field providers (fal, OpenAI, xAI)\nextract the media parts and flatten the text. Text is always sent\nverbatim: to reference inputs from the prompt, write the provider's own\nsyntax yourself (e.g. fal's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@Image1"},{"type":"text","value":", OpenAI's \"image 1\"). An array may\nbe media-only (e.g. upscalers or pure img2img endpoints that take no\ninstruction text)."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype MediaPrompt = string | MediaPromptPart[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:2109](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L2109)\n\nPrompt accepted by `generateImage()` / `generateVideo()`: a plain string,\nor an ordered array of content parts for image-conditioned generation\n(\"not like this *(image)*, more like this *(image)*\"). Part order is\nmeaningful — adapters with native multimodal prompts (Gemini, OpenRouter)\npreserve the interleaving; named-field providers (fal, OpenAI, xAI)\nextract the media parts and flatten the text. Text is always sent\nverbatim: to reference inputs from the prompt, write the provider's own\nsyntax yourself (e.g. fal's `@Image1`, OpenAI's \"image 1\"). An array may\nbe media-only (e.g. upscalers or pure img2img endpoints that take no\ninstruction text).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: MediaPrompt\ntitle: MediaPrompt\n---\n\n```ts\ntype MediaPrompt = string | MediaPromptPart[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:2109](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L2109)\n\nPrompt accepted by `generateImage()` / `generateVideo()`: a plain string,\nor an ordered array of content parts for image-conditioned generation\n(\"not like this *(image)*, more like this *(image)*\"). Part order is\nmeaningful — adapters with native multimodal prompts (Gemini, OpenRouter)\npreserve the interleaving; named-field providers (fal, OpenAI, xAI)\nextract the media parts and flatten the text. Text is always sent\nverbatim: to reference inputs from the prompt, write the provider's own\nsyntax yourself (e.g. fal's `@Image1`, OpenAI's \"image 1\"). An array may\nbe media-only (e.g. upscalers or pure img2img endpoints that take no\ninstruction text).\n"}
